  const translations = {
    en: {
      "h.kicker": "Hike · Valais · Swiss Alps",
      "h.title.em": "Siviez",
      "h.tag": "Turquoise reservoirs, an old high bisse, and alpine trails straight from the village door.",
      "h.stat.dist": "Distance", "h.stat.up": "Ascent", "h.stat.time": "Time", "h.stat.high": "High point", "h.stat.type": "Type", "h.stat.looptype": "Loop",
      "h.intro.lead": "Siviez sits at the end of the valley, right at the foot of the trails — so there's no drive to a trailhead, you just start walking. Below is our favourite day out, in full detail, plus a handful of other walks from the village.",
      "h.intro.body": "The star of the show is the big loop up to the two lakes: the Lac de Cleuson and, higher still, the Lac du Grand Désert — turquoise water, a mountain refuge, and a moon-like desert of stone at nearly 2750 metres. Here's everything you need to plan it, at any length.",
      "h.route.kicker": "Our favourite · The Grand Lac loop",
      "h.route.title": "Siviez – Combatseline – Lac de Cleuson – Lac du Grand Désert – Siviez",
      "h.route.sub": "The full loop, out and back to the village. All figures below are for the complete round trip.",
      "h.seg.kicker": "The full route", "h.seg.title": "Seven segments, one loop",
      "h.seg.intro": "The full route on foot, broken into its natural stages. Every shorter variant is just this list, cut off earlier and looped back to the chapel.",
      "h.seg.col.stage": "Stage", "h.seg.col.cum": "Cumul.",
      "h.seg.1": "Siviez → Combatseline", "h.seg.2": "Combatseline → flank of Lac de Cleuson", "h.seg.3": "Flank → bridge over the Printse", "h.seg.4": "Bridge → Refuge Saint-Laurent", "h.seg.5": "Saint-Laurent → Lac du Grand Désert", "h.seg.6": "Grand Désert → Chapelle Saint-Barthélémy", "h.seg.7": "Chapelle → Siviez", "h.seg.total": "Full loop",
      "h.var.kicker": "Choose your day", "h.var.title": "Five ways to walk it",
      "h.var.intro": "From a half-day out to the lake, to the full loop to the desert of stone. All variants start on foot from Siviez and return over the Cleuson dam past the chapel — except where you take the lift up.",
      "h.var.full.badge": "The full loop", "h.var.full.name": "To Lac du Grand Désert", "h.var.full.body": "The complete Grand Lac loop, all seven segments — Combatseline, the lake, the refuge, and the desert at 2746 m. A big, rewarding day.",
      "h.var.stl.badge": "Without the desert", "h.var.stl.name": "To Refuge Saint-Laurent", "h.var.stl.body": "Turn back at the refuge instead of climbing on to the Grand Désert. Still the lake, the bridge and lunch at 2500 m.",
      "h.var.bridge.badge": "Without the refuge", "h.var.bridge.name": "To the Printse bridge", "h.var.bridge.body": "Follow the lake to the dry-stone bridge over the Printse, then cut back to the chapel. A long but gentler day.",
      "h.var.lake.badge": "Shortest on foot", "h.var.lake.name": "To Lac de Cleuson", "h.var.lake.body": "Up to the flank of the lake — my favourite view — then straight back down to the chapel. The most accessible way to see the turquoise water.",
      "h.var.lift.badge": "Save the first climb", "h.var.lift.name": "Full loop, lift up", "h.var.lift.body": "Take the Combatseline chairlift from Siviez and skip the first 523 m of climbing. The full high loop, with far less effort to start.",
      "h.level.hard": "Demanding", "h.level.medhard": "Medium-hard", "h.level.medium": "Medium", "h.level.easy": "Accessible",
      "h.up.kicker": "The climb", "h.up.title": "Up to the lake",
      "h.up.p1": "On foot, the route leaves Siviez past the Auberge car park, picks up a footpath to Chalet Novelly, then joins the (mostly gravel) road up to the Combatseline lifts and its café. That first stretch is the steepest of the whole day — 523 metres of climb — which is exactly why the chairlift makes such a good shortcut.",
      "h.up.p2": "From the top station the path softens, traversing the flank above the Lac de Cleuson. This is the stretch I'd walk for the view alone: the whole turquoise lake below, the dam wall, and the peaks of the Grand Désert ahead.",
      "h.bridge.kicker": "Deeper in", "h.bridge.title": "The Printse bridge",
      "h.bridge.p1": "Past the lake, the trail drops to a dry-stone bridge over the young Printse river, then climbs again — steeper now — towards the refuge. This is where the big loop earns its name: the crowds thin out, and the landscape turns wild and mineral.",
      "h.bridge.p2": "If you're shortening the day, this is a natural turning point: cross back and follow the signs down to the chapel.",
      "h.ref.kicker": "Halfway · lunch", "h.ref.title": "Saint-Laurent",
      "h.ref.p1": "At 2500 metres, above the Cleuson dam, sits the Cabane Saint-Laurent — a mountain hut run by the local Ski-Club Arpettaz, and a genuinely lovely place to stop. Red parasols, deckchairs on the grass, and a terrace looking straight out over the lake.",
      "h.ref.p2": "It's the best spot on the route to eat properly, at a table: fondue, croûte, salads, soups and tarts, with running water, a WC and even a shower. It's usually staffed from the end of June to early September (in 2026: 3 July to 13 September).",
      "h.tip.label": "Puppy's tip",
      "h.ref.tip": "The refuge is seasonal, so don't count on it: carry enough water and a backup lunch anyway. When it's open, it's the highlight of the middle of the day. To be sure, reserve ahead by email at cabane@arpettaz.ch (there's no phone up there — lightning took out the mast).",
      "h.before.kicker": "Before you go", "h.before.title": "Come prepared",
      "h.before.early.t": "Start early", "h.before.early.b": "It's an 8-9 hour day. Leave Siviez in the morning so you're off the high, exposed sections well before any afternoon weather.",
      "h.before.water.t": "Carry water", "h.before.water.b": "Bring plenty — it's a long route and the refuge is seasonal. Don't rely on it being open; pack a backup lunch too.",
      "h.before.shoes.t": "Proper shoes", "h.before.shoes.b": "The upper sections are rocky and steep in places. Sturdy hiking boots with grip, not trainers.",
      "h.before.weather.t": "Check the weather", "h.before.weather.b": "This is high mountain terrain and it can turn quickly. Check the forecast the evening before and again in the morning.",
      "h.other.kicker": "More from Siviez", "h.other.title": "Other trails",
      "h.other.intro": "A few more walks that start from or near Siviez, from an easy family stroll to full alpine days. Distances and times are indicative — check current conditions before you set out.",
      "h.other.jp.name": "Japanese Garden via Siviez", "h.other.jp.body": "A circular hike to the \"Japanese Garden\", a natural setting on the glacier moraine towards Col des Gentianes.",
      "h.other.saxon.name": "Bisse de Saxon via Siviez", "h.other.saxon.body": "A long out-and-back along one of the region's historic bisses, with wide views over the Rhône valley.",
      "h.other.dent.name": "Dent de Nendaz – Tracouet – Balavaux", "h.other.dent.body": "A demanding loop over the Dent de Nendaz ridge, past Tracouet and the Balavaux hut, through forest and lakes.",
      "h.other.vieux.name": "Tortin – Haute-Nendaz via Bisse Vieux", "h.other.vieux.body": "An easy, mostly downhill walk along the Bisse Vieux beside the Printse — kid-friendly and shaded.",
      "h.cta.title": "Stay at the trailhead", "h.cta.body": "Every one of these walks starts a few minutes from Rosablanche C34 — dry your boots, rest your legs, and go again tomorrow.",
      "h.cta.stay": "See the apartment →", "h.cta.village": "Discover the village"
    },
    nl: {
      "h.kicker": "Wandelen · Valais · Zwitserse Alpen",
      "h.title.em": "Siviez",
      "h.tag": "Turquoise stuwmeren, een oude hoge bisse, en alpiene paden recht vanaf de dorpsdeur.",
      "h.stat.dist": "Afstand", "h.stat.up": "Stijging", "h.stat.time": "Tijd", "h.stat.high": "Hoogste punt", "h.stat.type": "Type", "h.stat.looptype": "Lus",
      "h.intro.lead": "Siviez ligt aan het einde van de vallei, recht aan de voet van de paden — dus geen rit naar een vertrekpunt, je begint gewoon te wandelen. Hieronder onze favoriete dagtocht, volledig uitgewerkt, plus een handvol andere wandelingen vanuit het dorp.",
      "h.intro.body": "De ster van de show is de grote lus omhoog naar de twee meren: het Lac de Cleuson en, nog hoger, het Lac du Grand Désert — turquoise water, een berghut, en een maanachtige steenwoestijn op bijna 2750 meter. Hier is alles wat je nodig hebt om het te plannen, op elke lengte.",
      "h.route.kicker": "Onze favoriet · The Grand Lac loop",
      "h.route.title": "Siviez – Combatseline – Lac de Cleuson – Lac du Grand Désert – Siviez",
      "h.route.sub": "De volledige lus, heen en terug naar het dorp. Alle cijfers hieronder gelden voor de complete rondwandeling.",
      "h.seg.kicker": "De volledige route", "h.seg.title": "Zeven segmenten, één lus",
      "h.seg.intro": "De volledige route te voet, opgedeeld in natuurlijke etappes. Elke kortere variant is gewoon deze lijst, vroeger afgebroken en terug naar de kapel.",
      "h.seg.col.stage": "Etappe", "h.seg.col.cum": "Cumul.",
      "h.seg.1": "Siviez → Combatseline", "h.seg.2": "Combatseline → flank Lac de Cleuson", "h.seg.3": "Flank → brugje over de Printse", "h.seg.4": "Brugje → Refuge Saint-Laurent", "h.seg.5": "Saint-Laurent → Lac du Grand Désert", "h.seg.6": "Grand Désert → Chapelle Saint-Barthélémy", "h.seg.7": "Kapel → Siviez", "h.seg.total": "Volledige lus",
      "h.var.kicker": "Kies je dag", "h.var.title": "Vijf manieren om het te doen",
      "h.var.intro": "Van een halve dag naar het meer, tot de volledige lus naar de steenwoestijn. Alle varianten starten te voet vanuit Siviez en keren terug over de Cleuson-dam langs de kapel — behalve waar je de lift omhoog neemt.",
      "h.var.full.badge": "De volledige lus", "h.var.full.name": "Naar Lac du Grand Désert", "h.var.full.body": "De complete Grand Lac loop, alle zeven segmenten — Combatseline, het meer, de refuge, en de woestijn op 2746 m. Een grote, lonende dag.",
      "h.var.stl.badge": "Zonder de woestijn", "h.var.stl.name": "Naar Refuge Saint-Laurent", "h.var.stl.body": "Keer terug bij de refuge in plaats van door te klimmen naar de Grand Désert. Nog steeds het meer, de brug en lunch op 2500 m.",
      "h.var.bridge.badge": "Zonder de refuge", "h.var.bridge.name": "Naar de Printse-brug", "h.var.bridge.body": "Volg het meer tot de droogstenen brug over de Printse, en snij dan terug naar de kapel. Een lange maar zachtere dag.",
      "h.var.lake.badge": "Kortste te voet", "h.var.lake.name": "Naar Lac de Cleuson", "h.var.lake.body": "Tot de flank van het meer — mijn favoriete uitzicht — en dan meteen terug naar de kapel. De meest toegankelijke manier om het turquoise water te zien.",
      "h.var.lift.badge": "Spaar de eerste klim", "h.var.lift.name": "Volledige lus, lift omhoog", "h.var.lift.body": "Neem de Combatseline stoeltjeslift vanuit Siviez en sla de eerste 523 m klim over. De volledige hoge lus, met veel minder moeite om te beginnen.",
      "h.level.hard": "Zwaar", "h.level.medhard": "Medium-zwaar", "h.level.medium": "Medium", "h.level.easy": "Toegankelijk",
      "h.up.kicker": "De klim", "h.up.title": "Omhoog naar het meer",
      "h.up.p1": "Te voet verlaat de route Siviez langs de parking van de Auberge, pikt een wandelpad op tot Chalet Novelly, en sluit dan aan op de (meestal onverharde) weg omhoog naar de Combatseline-liften en het café. Dat eerste stuk is het steilste van de hele dag — 523 hoogtemeters — en net daarom is de stoeltjeslift zo'n goede shortcut.",
      "h.up.p2": "Vanaf het bergstation wordt het pad zachter, dwars over de flank boven het Lac de Cleuson. Dit is het stuk dat ik voor het uitzicht alleen al zou lopen: het hele turquoise meer beneden, de dammuur, en de toppen van de Grand Désert vooruit.",
      "h.bridge.kicker": "Dieper de bergen in", "h.bridge.title": "De Printse-brug",
      "h.bridge.p1": "Voorbij het meer daalt het pad naar een droogstenen brug over de jonge Printse-rivier, en klimt dan weer — steiler nu — richting de refuge. Hier verdient de grote lus zijn naam: het volk dunt uit, en het landschap wordt wild en mineraal.",
